#32000
Serdim-ir-Lesk~
   A thick, gray mist envelops you as you make your way through the
murky waters of the Serdim-ir-Lesk.  This swamp is centuries old, said
to be the work of some ancient sorcery that turned a forest teeming with
life into a bleak, wet wasteland.  Old trees, their branches slick with
slime, lean crookedly out of the water, barely recognizable through the
mist.  You hear nothing but a penetrating silence.  The swamp continues
north and east.
~
