the endless wet mist and cling uncomfortably to you.  A bent-over tree
with black, sodden branches stands to the north.  Several fallen trees
block the way west, their gnarled limbs jutting dangerously out of the
black water.  Firm ground continues north and east, and the swamp lies
south.
