#32003
On Dry Land~
   You take your time here, glad of a little dry ground in the swamp.  A
large tree stands before you, its black branches dripping with the slime
of centuries; not a single leaf grows on its twisted limbs, nor lies on
the ground at its base.  The trunk must be five to seven feet around,
and a strange, sticky substance covers almost all of its branches.  You
could climb up, or go back south.
