you, hampering your vision.  Branches jut out of the swamp here and
there like the flailing arms of someone buried alive, reaching for life.
Half-sunken trees stand all about you, seemingly watching, the way
ghosts watch the living: silent and repressed.  The swamp stretches in
every direction.
