#32023
At the Gate of the Fortress~
   You stand before the gates to a primitive fortress built entirely
of wood.  You hear screams of anger at your intrusion as well as gasps
of wonder coming from within the wooden walls.  Two large towers stand to
either side of the gate with ropes which connect to the top of the gate
allowing the entrance to be shut quickly or opened easily.  The tops
of the wooden poles strung together to form the walls of the fortress
are shaved to a lethally sharp point to prevent intruders from climbing
over with ease.  Suddenly after a few moments of silence the gates open
for you slowly.  Within the gates you see a small, quaint village with
the furry, diminutive humanoids staring in awe at you.  Behind you a long
tunnel of trees leads back to the mystery of the Serdim-ir-Lesk Swamp.
~
