Out of the Chute, Into the Pool~
   You are flung out of the chute into the air, hit the water a second
or two later, skitter across the surface and finally come to rest,
floating gently on the pool.  To the north a grand waterfall plunges
into the pool from a rock face that rises several hundred feet into the
sky, deafening everything; its sheer power makes you realize how small
you really are.  The pool stretches out around you, and the chute
empties into it just to the east.
